Exact-exchange (EXX) run-time fixes for Quantum ESPRESSO 7.5
=============================================================

Applies to the qe-7.5 release source. Files changed:

    Modules/mp_exx.f90   sha256 before 012fd545051608820db79caa0a57b978e605eb8bd8183e16f9845f961e5ac51a
                         sha256 after  1f18defbf35cd85cab1503c6560ee3dc840c58153d0a6a1ea0d966e9f32d669d
    PW/src/exx.f90       sha256 before 9ce3e0fa836a11f6e3d8dda36ab92c1f39082fbf0587fc56a36fcc3f88b57bdf
                         sha256 after  bb818073569bebf28f1f24af1265d9b9b52522e862cd3f7888dc6a961c103894

Apply from the top of the source tree, before configure:

    patch -p1 < qe-7.5-exx-fixes.patch

Three changes. Each removes run time only; none changes a computed result.

1. Occupied-only exchange (exxinit, init_index_over_band). The exchange
   buffer and the partner-band loop stop at the highest occupied band.
   Stock code runs both over all nbnd bands and multiplies the empty
   partners by an occupation of zero after the FFT.
   This change adds two restrictions: fixed occupations only (smearing and
   tetrahedra stop with an error) and one band group (-nb 1).
2. exxinit, noncollinear GPU branch. The device-to-host copy of the whole
   exchange buffer moves from inside the band and k+q loops to once after
   the k loop.
3. vexx_k_gpu. The first and last partner band of each band are tabulated
   once per call. Stock code rescans all nbnd*m pair entries for every band
   inside the q and band-block loops. The CPU routine vexx_k contains the
   same scan and is NOT changed by this patch.

Status: not part of Quantum ESPRESSO; not submitted to or reviewed by its
developers. Tested on noncollinear spin-orbit HSE06 insulators. Tests and
timings are on the LORRAX manual page "HSE06 references with Quantum
ESPRESSO".

